WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.458
Hi! An English sentence starts with a capital letter and ends with a punctuation mark. Names need capitals too! Today we'll learn capital letters and punctuation.

2
00:00:13.608 --> 00:00:18.354
The first letter of every sentence is a capital: The cat is cute.

3
00:00:18.504 --> 00:00:21.426
The word I is always a capital.

4
00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:26.346
Names of people and places take capitals: Mei, Singapore.

5
00:00:26.496 --> 00:00:31.626
Days and months take capitals too: Monday, May.

6
00:00:31.776 --> 00:00:35.034
A telling sentence ends with a full stop.

7
00:00:35.184 --> 00:00:38.946
A question ends with a question mark: Where are you?

8
00:00:39.096 --> 00:00:44.418
Surprise or strong feeling takes an exclamation mark: What a big cake!

9
00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:51.282
Use commas to separate things in a list: apples, pears and grapes.

10
00:00:51.432 --> 00:00:55.674
Watch out! This sentence forgets three capitals!

11
00:00:55.824 --> 00:01:01.986
The start, My, the name, Peter, and the place, Singapore, all need capitals.

12
00:01:02.136 --> 00:01:07.242
Corrected: My friend Peter lives in Singapore.

13
00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:15.762
Your turn! Which is correct, A or B? Pause and think.

14
00:01:15.912 --> 00:01:21.882
The start and I need capitals, so B. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:22.032 --> 00:01:31.458
Another one! Where is my bag. Which mark goes at the end? Pause and think.

16
00:01:31.608 --> 00:01:37.314
It's a question, so a question mark. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:46.914
Here's another! What a tall tree. Which mark goes at the end? Pause and think.

18
00:01:47.064 --> 00:01:53.418
It shows surprise, so an exclamation mark. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.568 --> 00:02:04.890
Try one more! We went to malaysia. Apart from the first word, which word needs a capital? Pause and think.

20
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:11.250
Malaysia is a place, so it needs a capital. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:19.194
Try one more! Which one is correct? Pause and think.

22
00:02:19.344 --> 00:02:24.762
Days take capitals, so B. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:24.912 --> 00:02:35.778
Try one more! I bought eggs, ___, milk and bread. Which mark goes in the ___? Pause and think.

24
00:02:35.928 --> 00:02:41.082
A list uses commas. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:41.232 --> 00:02:50.946
Try one more! My sister is six. Which mark goes at the end? Pause and think.

26
00:02:51.096 --> 00:02:57.042
It's a telling sentence, so a full stop. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:57.192 --> 00:03:05.442
Last one! Which word needs a capital letter? Pause and think.

28
00:03:05.592 --> 00:03:12.377
Singapore is the name of a place, so it needs a capital. Did you get it right?

29
00:03:12.528 --> 00:03:23.609
Remember: capitals for the start, I, names, places, days and months. Full stops tell, question marks ask, and exclamation marks show feeling.

30
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:30.089
Write a sentence about your best friend and check the capitals and punctuation!

